      "worked_solution": "Since the sum of the measures of the interior angles of a triangle is $180^\\circ$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3z+4z+{40}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 7z+{40}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 7z & ={140}^{∘} \\\\ z & ={20}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠C & =4z \\\\  & =4({20}^{∘}) \\\\  & ={80}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
